5 23:23 CountyPublicSafetyRevolvingFunds.
6 I. A county may, by vote of the county convention, establish a county public safety revolving
7 fund for the provision of public safety services by county employees outside of the ordinary detail of
8 such persons, including but not limited to public safety services in connection with special events,
9 highwayconstruction, andother constructionprojects,or foranyother publicsafetypurposedeemed
10 appropriatebythecountysheriff.
11 II. Ifacountyestablishesacountypublicsafetyrevolvingfundforthepurposesidentifiedin
12 paragraphI, it shall deposit into thefund all or any part of the revenues from fees, charges, or other
13 income derived from the activities or services supported by the fund to replenish the fund to the
14 original appropriated amount. The county shall deposit any other revenues approved by the county
15 convention into the revolving fund, provided that funds in excess of the original appropriated
16 amount shall be deposited into the general fund. The money in the fund shall be allowed to
17 accumulate from year to year. The county treasurer shall have custody of all moneys in the fund,
18 and shall pay out the same only upon order of the county commissioners. Such funds shall be
19 expendedonlyforthepurposesforwhichthefundwascreated.
20 III. The county convention may, at the time it establishes a county public safety revolving
21 fund or at any time thereafter, place limitations on expenditures from the fund including, but not
22 limited to, restrictions on the types of items or services that may be purchased from the fund. No
23 amount may be expended from a revolving fund established hereunder for any item or service for
24 whichanappropriationhasbeenspecificallyrejectedbythecountyconventionduringthesameyear.
25 IV. The provisions of this section shall not preclude the establishment of a county public
26 safetyrevolvingfundforanyotherpurposeauthorizedbylaw.

